{"type": "message", "message": "For a small flat, **minimalistic means keeping what’s useful and meaningful, while giving it room to breathe**—not making your home empty or all-white.\n\n- **Purposeful furniture:** fewer well-chosen pieces, sized for the room.\n- **Clear routes:** easy movement between doors, seating and storage.\n- **Less visual clutter:** closed storage for everyday things, with a few favourites on display.\n- **A simple palette:** a few complementary colours and materials.\n- **Warmth:** wood, soft textiles and personal touches keep it welcoming.\n\nYour proposed sage walls fit the simple-palette idea, but paint alone doesn’t make a room minimalist. Practical storage and a comfortable layout matter just as much.", "conversationId": "4e7c2f392feb4f428de4e14a22303266"}
